# Build context hygiene. Two reasons, and the second one is a correctness problem rather than a
# speed problem:
#   1. the host's build output is several GB and none of it is a build input;
#   2. COPY would otherwise carry the host's obj/ into the image, and the files there
#      (project.assets.json, the generated MSBuild files) hold absolute Windows paths such as
#      C:\Users\... - the in-container restore then reads assets pointing outside the container and
#      fails in a way that reads like a code error rather than a context error.
**/bin/
**/obj/
_publish_tmp/
Novara_Publish/
.vs/
.vscode/
.git/
.gitignore
*.user
**/__pycache__/
node_modules/

# Desktop-only trees. Novara.Server references Novara.Sync.Server, which references Novara.Core -
# nothing else in the repository is compiled for the image.
Novara.Tests/
NovaraMCP/
StickNoteHost/
Pages/
Services/
Themes/
Assets/
DiaryEditorJs/
Installer/
Tools/
deploy/
memory/

# Documentation and the desktop project's own files.
*.md
*.slnx
app.manifest
App.xaml
App.xaml.cs
AppResources.cs
IconData.cs
MainWindow.xaml
MainWindow.xaml.cs
Novara.csproj
ProbeDataSet.json
